WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.920
The year is 1968.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.760
A seven year old boy, named Clay, has just finished building a contraption

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.720
that remotely opens and closes

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.280
a little outside door for his family's dog.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.480
He's constantly building toys and mechanical contraptions like this one

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.900
Using spare bike parts, old TVs, radios and any other objects that he can get his hands on.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.140
8 years later, the year is 1976.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.200
The first personal computers hit the market.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.300
Clay, now 15, finds himself immediately drawn

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.155
to the the newly developing industry of computers.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.400
He soon begins creating software programs

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.540
and has a unique way of understanding how technology, and humans, can interact.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.040
Throughout his adolescence,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.560
because of this interest to understanding and his natural ingenuity,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.260
Clay creates and sells several computer softwares,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.800
develops a software business,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.040
appears on TV about a dozen times,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.060
meets the president and graduates from M.I.T.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.540
The year is 1982.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.000
Clay is 21.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.960
Clay loses his mother to coronary heart disease.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.860
Having not had a father in the picture,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.240
Clay's mother was one of the few people Clay had

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.680
that he truly loved and could count on his life.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.640
Clay struggles with his mother's death

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.540
the experience and idea of her death,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.680
and death in general,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.040
makes no sense to him.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.580
Clay wonders why a conscious intelligent being,

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.480
unlike any other species,

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.900
dies like every other species.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.920
How can a species, that can create fire, tools, computers, airplanes, rockets, medicine and so on

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.820
still die basicaly the same, as a slug or a lizard.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.600
Early on, Clay forms the belief that it doesn't have to be this way.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.860
He believes, that in a not so far future,

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.800
we can overcome the dependence on our weak and entropic biological human body through technology.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.300
Clay embarks on his pursuit of this belief.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.680
He studies and develops his theories and begins to immerse further and further

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.980
into newly emerging computer software and biotechnologies.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.980
The year is 1997.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.340
At age 36,

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.780
Clay starts a biotech company named Kurve

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:01.340
which creates algorithms and computer models related to human biology and genetics.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:06.620
Clay soon discovers that the brain is quite similar to the softwares he's creating and studying the brain with.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.640
The brain recognizes patterns,

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.760
organizes these patterns hierarchically,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.620
and is then able to formulate an awareness of its conditions

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.120
and make judgements accordingly.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.700
Just like the newly developing artificialy intelligent softwares Clay is working with.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.120
In this, Clay realizes that if the coding of human consciousness can be fully modelled and replicated

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.260
it could also be, theoretically,

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.840
placed onto device of replicable function

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.540
and sustained indefinitely.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.100
In other words, the human experience of self

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.020
could essentially be limitless beyond the human body.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.680
32 years later.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.680
The year is 2029.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:48.100
At age 68, Clay and his biotech company successfully reverse engineered the entire function of the human brain.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.080
This, in combination with a vast array of other innovations in the biotechnology space,

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.060
now means that human consciousness can be enhanced,

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.120
maintained

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:57.840
and transferred

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.340
through and onto any hardware device or cloud service entity.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.860
People now have the opportunity to think and understand

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.880
at a rate that is exponentially greater than any conceived possibility of the past.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.840
Mental conditions are now able to be modified beyond inherited genetics.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.460
Lifelong mental disorders can be erradicated.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.100
Bacterial and age related diseases can be circumvented.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.520
8 years later.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.200
Clay is now 76.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.400
The year is 2037.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:30.460
Clay is the first person to successfully upload his entire brain function to an outisde hybrid entity.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:31.940
Now, at any point,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.700
Clay can change over to a separate synthetic body

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:38.660
and reconnect to his consciousness via a software access server,

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.620
like the Cloud,

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.520
and still remain with his sense of self.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.040
With this Clay would lead humanity into a new realm of existence.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.380
A life of boundless consciousness.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.560
The year is 2486.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:55.640
Clay, along with the rest of humanity lives hundreds of years past their previously standard life expectancy.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.560
Clay travels the whole world and visits every place there is to see.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.700
He reads every book.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:01.800
Sees every movie.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.060
Watches every video.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:08.180
Visits every website, masters every language, hears every story and learns every skill.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:09.620
He falls into love

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:10.660
and out of love,

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.020
over and over.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.180
Hundreds of years turn to thousands,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.820
thousands turns to millions.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.020
The year becomes irrelevant.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.360
Every time boredom, overpopulation, overconsumption and so on

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.920
appear to be on the horizon.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.960
New worlds are discovered and created.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.660
Clay explores, new planets, new galaxies, new dimensions.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.580
He meets new beings from other worlds.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.180
New realms of art, science and entertainment emerge and die.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:36.940
Emerge and die.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.040
He experiences new types of feelings,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.280
new ways of thinking,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.980
new ways of experiencing.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.440
Millions and millions more years go by.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.380
Clay's home, his mother, his sister, his dog, his childhood, his mortal self,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.460
the conditions of the worlds he was born in

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.100
have all long been forgotten.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.400
Stored away, like an old file, on an old hardrive

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.540
he forgot he ever had.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.380
Clay continues on for millions of years.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.360
He explores more worlds and more realms of life... On and on.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.640
Until, eventually,

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.220
the stars begin to die,

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.060
the galaxies begin to dissolve

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.080
and the universe begins to burn out.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:15.060
Clay accomplish what had been but a fantasy for all of human history before him,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.240
a supremacy over one's nature,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.520
an immortality.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:19.940
He travelled the cosmos,

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.340
he made millions and millions of discoveries,

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.020
learned everything there was to know:

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.100
every law of physics,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.700
every rule of reality,

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.080
all to end up here,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.200
about to die,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.420
with everything else.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:31.980
"What was it all for?"

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.240
Clay wonders to himself.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.260
What was the point of beating his own death,

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.880
just to be subjected to the death of the universe?

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.020
How could a species that transcended its own biology

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.620
and the nature of life itself,

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:47.220
just to die off with the universe, like all the little particles and amoebas that came before it?

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:50.160
In the remaining moments of this smothering universe,

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.560
Clay decides to create one last thing.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.680
Now, having learned all the mechanics of nature and how the universe works,

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.940
Clay begins to construct a blueprint for a new one.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.180
Like creating the rules of a videogame:

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.400
he renders the code

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.740
for a new universe.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.980
He makes it hard but not impossible.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.680
Long but not without end.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.520
He makes it so that each level gets a little more complex, yet a little more interesting.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.140
A little more daunting yet a little more rewarding.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.040
He makes so the rules of the universe change a little overtime,

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.280
never too far so it makes no sense,

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.820
but never too close that it makes complete sense.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.440
He hides the endgame so far from the starting point,

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.500
only in the final stage can it be seen and comprehended.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.700
He conceals the truth amidst the chaos,

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.440
the logic amidst the disorder,

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.800
the meaning amidst the lack thereof.

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:35.580
Finally,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.500
he leaves the possibility for creating anew.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:39.780
Clay finishes.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:40.800
"It's perfect."

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.060
he says to himself.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.240
The universe begins to compress tighter and tighter,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.900
the dying energy dries out any remaining life,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.660
the last stars turn off,

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.340
the last planets explode.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.660
Everything gives one last node a farewell, to this existence,

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.900
as it squeezes back into nothingness.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.500
As the energy tightens into a final pinpoint,

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.580
Clay's new universe explodes.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.840
A bursting of color, matter and energy

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.620
floods out, reversing the nothing into an ever expanding everything.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.600
Time and space begin again.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.980
Stars fill the sky.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.460
Celestial collisions occur.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:13.460
Planets Form.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.720
Bacteria and amoebas flow around each other.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.260
Life emerges

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.760
and the trial and error of existence unfolds.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.640
A sequence of living and dying,

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:22.780
trying and failing,

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.180
evolving and adapting,

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:25.500
thinking and talking,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.120
building and creating.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.340
Years, and years, and years would go by.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:32.980
The year...

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.380
...is 1968.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.640
A seven year old boy named Clay

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.140
has just finished building a contraption

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.140
that remotely opens and closes

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.420
a little outside door for his family's dog.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:46.060
He's constantly building toys and mechanical contraptions like this one

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:51.900
Using spare bike parts, old TVs, radios and any other objects that he can get his hands on.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.280
He'll probably do a lot in this life.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:56.920
As clay finishes the dogs door,

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.180
his sister asks him:

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.460
"Didn't you already make that?"

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.100
"Yeah. I just took it apart and made it again",

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.140
replies Clay.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:03.960
"Why?",

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.060
asks his sister.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:05.940
"I don't know.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:08.100
It was fun and i wanted to see if i could make it better",

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.320
replies Clay.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.760
"Well, is it better now?",

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.200
asks his sister.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.600
Clay replies:

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.660
"No. It was fine".

